# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DAD'S FIELD NOTEBOOK · 180 pages · 18 subjects x 10 districts
#
#   Creator: "make them more mythic. write them in present tense from the past.
#   true notes to self. use the codex to figure out lore bearings."
#
# ★ THE THREE RULES, and they are rules because the old pass broke all three.
#
#   1 · PRESENT TENSE FROM THE PAST. He is writing IN the moment, and the moment
#       has already gone. "I am counting the wicks" — not "I counted them."
#       The reader arrives years late to a man who is still standing there.
#
#   2 · NOTES TO SELF. Not letters. Seven pages of the old set said "son" and
#       that is a different document — it makes him an author addressing an
#       audience, which is the opposite of a private notebook. He argues with
#       himself, corrects himself, tells himself to write things down. Nobody is
#       being spoken to. That is what makes reading them feel like trespass.
#
#   3 · MYTHIC, EARNED BY OBSERVATION. He is a beastologist. The awe comes from
#       what he MEASURES, not from adjectives — he takes the temperature of warm
#       ground, counts nine characters, times a bind at one and a half seconds.
#       A naturalist who has walked into scripture and keeps taking notes anyway.
#
# ★ THE ARC IS THE DISTRICT ORDER. Malezor is a rumour in a schoolyard;
#   Korathen is the answer, and the answer costs him something. Ten depths of
#   one question, so a player who chases a single subject outward gets it
#   answered properly and a player who sweeps one district gets ten questions
#   opened at once.
#
# ★ Lore anchored to the codex in memory: 63 Astralites (9 families x 7 tiers)
#   plus AETHRYX, 27 worlds with Zyraxis as Ax-9, the 16 Prisms, the ten
#   Gemlords and the Empty Throne, the Seers under Xenoxil, Cytherion and the
#   Bug War, the Migration, Thardun, Dreamland. Where the record is silent these
#   EXTEND rather than contradict — and they are extensions, to be ratified
#   before they reach the Master Codex.
#
#   EDIT HERE, then run:  python3 tools/sync_scrolls.py
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
T = [
("THE ASTRALITE MATRIX","matrix",[
 "Every living thing here carries a signature. The bull, the boy driving it, the grass they are standing in. Twenty years I have looked for one exception. Tonight I stop looking, and I write down that I stopped.",
 "Zarvane. The oasis readers name the signature before the animal comes over the dune. I ask to be taught. The old one says you cannot teach a man to have been born here. He is not being cruel. He is being accurate.",
 "Andrannor, past the clubs. A splicer holds one signature in two shapes and the room applauds. Something pays for the second shape. It is not the splicer. I do not know who, and I am writing it down so that I cannot later pretend I am not watching it happen.",
 "Veridan. The root-scribes count nine families in the lattice and will not say how they counted. Only that the ninth family counts you back. I am sitting under a tree that is older than my language, being counted.",
 "Netharion, sixth week in the archive. Nine families. Seven tiers. Sixty-three. There is a sixty-fourth line ruled on the page and no ink has ever stayed on it. I try. It beads and runs like water off oil.",
 "Vorashil. I give the embassy my sixty-fourth theory and they are kind about it. Then a student corrects me in the corridor: the sixty-fourth is not a fourth anything. It is what the other sixty-three are measured against.",
 "Xilnar. The dead still carry signature. I check three times because I do not want it to be true. The Matrix is not a property of being alive. It is a property of having been. I sit with that a week and it does not soften.",
 "Baelgor. I read the Founders' Pledge again with the notation in my head and the poetry falls off it like bark. They are not being reverent. They are filing a claim, and the claim is on something that was already occupied.",
 "Thardin. Their instruments write to the lattice now. The Ministry calls it manufacture. Every older word I own for it means forgery. I keep the file numbers in the back of this book in case the numbers are all that survives.",
 "Korathen. Last page on this. The Matrix is not a map of what exists. It is the list of what is permitted to exist. Someone wrote the list. I have come a long way to say I would like a word, and there is no one at the desk."]),

("THE TWENTY-SEVEN WORLDS","worlds",[
 "There is a counting rhyme in the Malezor schoolyard that ends at twenty-seven. I ask four teachers what it counts. I get four shrugs and one long look. It is the look I write down.",
 "Zarvane. The readers say the sky holds twenty-seven true stars and everything else is weather. I laugh before I can stop myself. Nobody laughs with me, and the silence goes on long enough to become an answer.",
 "Andrannor. The slang for a hopeless errand is 'ask the twenty-seventh.' No one can tell me why it is funny. It stops being funny to me somewhere between the third bar and the fourth.",
 "Veridan Seedvault. Three specimens in the cold room grew under a different sun. The labels give a number where a origin should be. Ours is nine. Nobody in this building finds that strange, which is the strangest part.",
 "Netharion. There it is in the Null Observatory, ruled and plain as a debt ledger. Twenty-seven worlds, ordered — and not by distance. We are Ax-9. I read it four times standing up.",
 "Vorashil. Every visitor arrives already knowing our number and all of them are a little disappointed by it. Nine is apparently not an interesting position. I have stopped asking what an interesting one would be.",
 "Xilnar. The Blackwake Chapel keeps twenty-seven wicks for the dead of worlds that are not this one. Six have gone out. I count them twice. Nobody relights them and nobody will tell me which six.",
 "Baelgor. The University teaches the Expanse as history, not astronomy. The worlds were not discovered. They were assigned. I write that down and my hand is not steady, and I am fifty-one years old.",
 "Thardin. The Anomaly Engine can hear the other twenty-six. The Ministry logs it as industrial noise and files it unopened. I have copied the file numbers. Somebody after me may have the standing I do not.",
 "Korathen. Twenty-seven is not a count of places. It is a count of attempts. Nine are still running. I do not know what became of the other eighteen and I am very much afraid that I do."]),

("AETHRYX","aethryx",[
 "Kelthor says the word once in twenty years and will not say it twice. He tells me it is not a word for a beastwarden's mouth. He has never refused me anything else, and he does not look at me for the rest of the day.",
 "Zarvane. The elders bow their heads before they say it. I ask three of them why and none can tell me. The reflex is older than the reason it came from. That happens with true things and with nothing else.",
 "Andrannor. They use it as a curse in the clubs, cheerfully, all night. The oldest patrons still flinch. Habit outlives belief out here, and habit is the more honest witness.",
 "Veridan. Parliament records the name in a script used for nothing else and taught to no one living. I copy nine characters by lamplight. I have never found the tenth and I have looked in four districts.",
 "Netharion. The Impossible Archive is blunt where everyone else has been careful: AETHRYX is not one of the sixty-three. It is the reason there are sixty-three. The sentence is unsigned and the ink is older than the shelf.",
 "Vorashil, Unmouth Academy. It is not a being with a signature. It is the condition under which a signature is possible at all. It takes me a month to be able to write that sentence down without my hand arguing.",
 "Xilnar. The dead do not fear it. I have turned that over more than anything else in this notebook and I still do not like where it goes. Fear is for things that can still do something to you.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge was sworn to something and the founders never wrote what. The blank is exactly nine letters wide. I measure it twice with a rule, in a library, like a madman, and I am right both times.",
 "Thardin. They try to instrument it. Every device returns the reading it was built expecting. Every time, in every hand. That is not how an instrument behaves. That is how a mirror behaves.",
 "Korathen. The Gemlords do not claim to serve AETHRYX. They claim to have been noticed by it. Once. Each. That is the entire foundation of their authority, and having met one, I find it sufficient."]),

("THE GEMLORDS","gemlords",[
 "Rakoron sleeps under our feet and the ground above him is warm in winter. Kelthor says that is not a figure of speech. I take the temperature myself, in three places, in January. It is not a figure of speech.",
 "Zarvane. Ivirium's pearl-light is why the night here is never wholly dark. The oasis remembers being watched. Their word for dusk translates as 'the looking', and they use it without ceremony, the way we say evening.",
 "Andrannor. There is a Gemlord under this district too and the clubs are built directly over the seam. Nobody mentions it. I think that is not disrespect. I think it is the only way to live on top of one.",
 "Veridan. The root-scribes will not write a Gemlord's name in ink that can be erased. Everything else here is written in something that fades on purpose. I ask what they are afraid of forgetting. Wrong question, they say.",
 "Netharion. Ten seats in the ledger. Ten districts, ten Gemlords, one to a place, and the ledger is not a list of rulers. It is a list of what each place is anchored by. Remove the anchor and the entry does not become empty. It becomes false.",
 "Vorashil. The embassy explains the Gemlords as a treaty. It is a good explanation and it is wrong. A treaty is between parties who could have refused. Nobody here was ever asked.",
 "Xilnar. The dead speak of theirs in the present tense. So do I now, and I do not remember deciding to. The grammar of this district gets into you within a week and it does not come out.",
 "Baelgor. They keep a hall with ten doors, nine of them in use. I stand in front of the tenth for most of an afternoon. The hinges are worn. Something has opened it, more than once, and not recently.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry has a department for Gemlord relations. It has a budget, a letterhead, and no recorded meeting in ninety years. The budget goes up annually. I find that more frightening than a monster.",
 "Korathen. I have now been in the presence of one. I am not going to write what was said. I will write this: it is not that they are powerful. It is that they are earlier, and everything since has been arranged around them."]),

("WHAT A ZYREX IS","zyrex",[
 "The Malezor farmers say beast for anything with four legs and Zyrex for anything that looks back. That is not a taxonomy. After twenty years in the field it is also not wrong.",
 "Zarvane. A Zyrex will refuse a bond it does not want and starve rather than take it. I have watched this happen and I could not intervene. Whatever they are, they are not livestock, and I will not write the word again.",
 "Andrannor. The splicers here treat a Zyrex as a chassis. It works. The animal survives, performs, and comes back wrong in a way that no instrument I own can name and every child in the room can see.",
 "Veridan. The root-scribes divide the living into those that carry a signature and those that ARE one. A Zyrex is the second kind. I write that down and then sit for an hour not writing anything else.",
 "Netharion. The archive is precise: never Humanoid-primary. Creature, then Beast, then Draconic — the ladder is not power, it is DISTANCE FROM US. Every rung further from a hand that could hold a pen.",
 "Vorashil. A student asks me whether a Zyrex is an animal or a person. I say the question is malformed. She asks what the well-formed question is. I have been working on it since and I am not close.",
 "Xilnar. The dead ones still answer. Not to a name — to a bond. Whatever is bound when you bond a Zyrex, it is not the body, because the body is here and it is empty and something still turned toward me.",
 "Baelgor. The University teaches that Zyrex were made. The oldest text in their own basement says they were ADMITTED. Two words, one syllable apart, and an entire theology between them.",
 "Thardin. They can now build something that satisfies every test for a Zyrex. It passes all of them. It does not look back. I write that as a technical finding because I cannot write it as anything else without shaking.",
 "Korathen. What a Zyrex is: a shape the Matrix permits, holding itself together on purpose. That is also the best definition I have of a person. I have spent my life on this and the answer will not stay on one side of the line."]),

("THE VERDANT AWAKENING","verdant",[
 "Something happened to the green here before there were people to see it. The Malezor hedgerows grow in patterns that repeat at a scale no hedgerow needs. I sketch four. They are the same four everywhere.",
 "Zarvane. Even the oasis growth carries it — and the oasis should be the youngest green on the planet. It is not young. It is only recently watered.",
 "Andrannor. The Awakening is a drinking story here, told badly, and every bad telling keeps the same three details. Corruption of a story loses ornament first. Those three details are load-bearing.",
 "Veridan. This is where it happened, and the district does not celebrate it. The root-scribes call it the Waking and lower their voices, and they lower them the way you do in a sickroom, not a temple.",
 "Netharion. The archive links the Awakening to the Viridian creatures directly — not as descendants. As by-products. Something woke up and these walked out of the process, unasked for and alive.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy argues about whether the Awakening was an event or a decision. I have stood in the place it happened. It was a decision. I cannot prove it and I will not be talked out of it.",
 "Xilnar. Nothing that died before the Awakening answers. Nothing. The dead here have a horizon and it is dated. I check it against three other records and it holds to the season.",
 "Baelgor. The founders arrived after, and built their whole claim on ground that had already agreed to something else. The Pledge reads differently once you know it is a second signature on an occupied page.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry is trying to induce a small one. Controlled. Local. A pilot programme with a permit number. I have read the permit. There is no line on the form for what wakes up.",
 "Korathen. The Verdant Awakening was not the world coming alive. The world was already alive. It was the world becoming AWARE that it was, and there is no evidence anywhere that it has gone back to sleep."]),
("THE SIXTEEN PRISMS","prisms",[
 "Kelthor keeps a chip of something in a cloth in a drawer and will not tell me what it is a chip OF. He lets me hold it once. It is not cold and it is not warm. It is the temperature of my own hand, exactly, and it stays that way.",
 "Zarvane. Sixteen is a sacred number here and nobody sells it as one. It is in the tilework, the meal, the way a caravan divides. Sacred numbers you can buy are decoration. This one is load-bearing.",
 "Andrannor. A collector shows me two Prism fragments and asks which is worth more. Neither, I say, they are the same substance. He laughs. Then he tells me only one of them can be sold, and will not say which or why.",
 "Veridan. The scribes say a Prism is not a stone. It is an ERUPTION that has stopped moving. Nothing here is described by what it is. Everything is described by what it was doing when it stopped.",
 "Netharion. Sixteen Prisms, sixteen Astralite Prisms, one list. They are the same objects under two names, and both names are older than the archive. Nobody renamed anything. Two peoples arrived at the same sixteen.",
 "Vorashil. A Prism cannot be crafted. The Academy is clear, and slightly offended by the question. You can refine downward from one forever. You cannot climb back up. Nothing in this world can make one, and sixteen exist.",
 "Xilnar. The dead know the count too. Sixteen. They do not know why and they have had a great deal of time to wonder. That is the first thing on this journey to genuinely frighten me.",
 "Baelgor. One Prism is named. The Key of Anciuxor. The other fifteen are described, located, revered, and left nameless, and the omission is consistent across four archives that never met.",
 "Thardin. They have modelled a seventeenth. The mathematics is sound and complete and the Ministry is delighted. Nothing has ever answered it. I do not think the mathematics is wrong. I think sixteen is a decision, not a limit.",
 "Korathen. The Prisms are not artefacts of the world. They are the world's terms and conditions, made portable. Sixteen conditions. Everything that lives here lives inside all sixteen, and only one of them has a name."]),

("THE BONDING VESSELS","vessels",[
 "A Malezor child hands me a Zysphere and tells me it is 'for keeping'. I ask keeping what. She thinks about it seriously, the way children do, and says: the agreeing.",
 "Zarvane. One sphere, one attempt, win or lose. Nobody here finds that harsh. A man tells me a bargain you can retry was never a bargain, and goes back to his tea.",
 "Andrannor. There is a market in used spheres and I cannot find anyone who will explain what used means. A sphere that has held something is worth less. Nobody will say what it is worth less TO.",
 "Veridan. The scribes will not call it catching. They call it the offering, and the offering is made by the sphere, not the thrower. I have been holding it backwards for twenty years.",
 "Netharion. There is one kind of Zysphere. The tiered names in the old catalogues are a merchant's fiction — the tiers were never spendable and never were. One kind. It has always been one kind.",
 "Vorashil. A sphere opens on contact and takes about one and a half seconds to bind. The Academy times it to the hundredth. In that second and a half something is decided, and the decision is not the thrower's.",
 "Xilnar. A sphere that has held a Zyrex that has since died still weighs the same and no longer opens. I have three on the table in front of me. None of them will open. I do not think they are broken.",
 "Baelgor. The University teaches sphere-craft as engineering. In the basement there is a text that teaches it as courtship, and the diagrams are identical. Only the verbs differ.",
 "Thardin. Thardin makes them. That is the whole of Thardun's business and the source of its reach — every district on this world depends on a Thardinian object to complete the oldest relationship it has.",
 "Korathen. The vessel does not capture. It witnesses. Two things agree and the sphere is what makes the agreement binding on a world where agreements are otherwise weather. Somebody built a courthouse the size of a fist."]),

("CYTHERION","cytherion",[
 "The Malezor grain has an insect in it that no farmer here can name and every farmer here knows to leave alone. It is not native. Nobody remembers being told that. Everybody knows.",
 "Zarvane. The oasis has a story about a war in the sky between a spider and a mantis, told to children to explain why you do not kill either. It is a nursery rhyme with a body count.",
 "Andrannor. The Alienlands begin somewhere north of here and no map agrees where. The border is not a line. It is a gradient, and I have watched the local insects change over four miles of walking.",
 "Veridan. The Seedvault holds specimens from planet eight and labels them honestly. Cytherion. I ask how they got here. The answer is: they walked, which cannot be true, and is.",
 "Netharion. Planet eight, the Bug War, Spider against Mantis, and the Grid that came out of it. The archive treats the Grid as the war's only surviving institution. Not its victor. Its institution.",
 "Vorashil. A scholar tells me the Migration was not an invasion. Cytherion lost and the losers walked to the ninth world. Everything in the Alienlands is descended from a defeat, and it has been very patient.",
 "Xilnar. Their dead are here too, and they are not confused about which world they are on. They know exactly where they are. They simply have not agreed to be from here.",
 "Baelgor. Nothing in the University's history of Zyraxis mentions Cytherion, and the omission is too clean to be an oversight. Somebody edited. I would like to know what the first draft said.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry has reverse-engineered Grid architecture and does not know that is what it has. I recognise it from a Netharion plate. I am not going to be the one to tell them.",
 "Korathen. Cytherion is the eighth world and we are the ninth, and the order is not arbitrary. Whatever ran the attempt on eight, watched, learned, and ran it again here. We are the revision."]),

("THE SEERS","seers",[
 "A Malezor family is short one child this season and the village has agreed on a story about a fall. I have seen the ground they say she fell from. I write the family's name here and nothing else.",
 "Zarvane. The readers can tell when one has passed through. Not by sight. By a gap — a stretch of road where the signatures thin out for a day and then fill back in, like water closing.",
 "Andrannor. They recruit here. Openly, in the good clubs, with excellent manners. Nobody stops them because nobody can name what the offence would be until it is far too late to name it.",
 "Veridan. The Seers want the Fathergems and Parliament knows and Parliament is negotiating. I sit in the gallery for two days. Nobody says the word taken. They say reallocated.",
 "Netharion. The archive has it plainly: the taken are not hostages. They are offerings. The name under the whole arrangement is Xenoxil, and the page it appears on has been rebound at least twice.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy has a lecture on Seer doctrine and it is very good and it is very careful, and at no point in ninety minutes does anyone ask what happens to the children. I ask. The room waits for the next question.",
 "Xilnar. The taken do not arrive here. That is the whole of the finding and it took me three weeks. Everyone else who dies on this world comes to Xilnar. Theirs go somewhere else.",
 "Baelgor. The Seers replaced something older and kept its buildings. The Pledge-era orders had a word for what they were guarding against, and the Seers now use that same word for themselves.",
 "Thardin. They have Ministry contracts. Filed, numbered, legal. The most dangerous thing I have found in ten years is not a monster. It is correct paperwork.",
 "Korathen. The Seers are not a faith and not an army. They are a supply chain. Everything else — the robes, the doctrine, the commanders — is logistics wearing vestments, and it runs the whole length of this world."]),

("THE NOVARIAN CHALLENGE","novarian",[
 "Kelthor mentions a name, Novarius, and then talks about the weather for ten minutes. He is not evading. He is deciding, and by the time he has decided I have stopped being owed the answer.",
 "Zarvane. There is a trial here that nobody has completed in living memory and it is not advertised. You are told about it only after you would already have passed some earlier part of it.",
 "Andrannor. The Challenge is a boast in the clubs. Everyone has an uncle who attempted it. Nobody has an uncle who came back and described it, and both halves of that are said in the same breath.",
 "Veridan. The scribes say Novarius was the first Beast Master, and that first does not mean earliest. It means the one the others are measured against. There is no second on any list I have found.",
 "Netharion. The archive keeps the Challenge as an open record — not history, not legend. Open. As in still running. As in a thing you could enter this year.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy will explain the Challenge's structure but not its purpose. When I press, a professor says the purpose is not withheld from me. It is withheld from everyone, and it always has been.",
 "Xilnar. Novarius is not among the dead. I look properly, with help, over eleven days. He is not here, and I am told with some care that this does not mean he is alive.",
 "Baelgor. The University holds that the Challenge is how this world proves it is worth continuing. I write that down and then cannot eat dinner, because I have read what happens on the worlds that stopped.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry would like to standardise the Challenge. There is a working group. Twelve years, no report. Some things will not sit still to be measured and this is the largest of them.",
 "Korathen. The Seers do not want to win the Novarian Challenge. They want to end it. If the Challenge is how the world proves itself, then ending it is not conquest. It is a verdict entered by default."]),

("THE RIZER PATH","rizer",[
 "Every Malezor child says they will be a Rizer. Their parents smile. Nobody explains what a Rizer actually is, and I am starting to think nobody in this village can, including me, and I am one.",
 "Zarvane. The path is not taught here. It is recognised. An elder watches a girl fail a task badly and says, that one. I ask how he knows. He says she did not look at anyone before she tried again.",
 "Andrannor. You can buy the equipment, the licence and the coat. There is no market anywhere in this district for the thing itself, and men who own all three keep asking me where to get it.",
 "Veridan. The scribes hold that Rizer is not a profession but a DIRECTION. You do not become one. You are pointed, and then it is a question of whether you keep walking.",
 "Netharion. Humanoid and Zyrex Prime run on one system. The archive is unambiguous. Zyrex evolve and humanoids RIZE, and it is the same ladder viewed from two ends. I have been climbing without knowing the name of the stair.",
 "Vorashil. A Rizer's ceiling is Immortal. That is not a metaphor for excellence — it is a tier, with a number, on a chart that also contains creatures. The Academy shows me the chart the way you show someone a diagnosis.",
 "Xilnar. The dead Rizers still carry their rank. Whatever rising is, it is not something you hold. It is something that happens to what you are, and it survives you.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge was sworn by Rizers. Not soldiers, not founders — Rizers, and the distinction is made three times in the first paragraph by people who were not wasting ink.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry certifies Rizers now. There is an examination and a fee. Everyone I have met with a certificate has needed it, and everyone I have met who did not need it has never sat the examination.",
 "Korathen. The Rizer path is the world's own immune response. Something is coming for this place, and the path is how Zyraxis grows people capable of standing in front of it. I have been part of an immune system my whole life and I only now know it."]),
("THE TWENTY TYPES","types",[
 "The Malezor almanac lists twelve types and the farmers use nine of them. Both numbers are wrong and both numbers work, which tells me the truth is not something you need in order to farm.",
 "Zarvane. The readers work in twenty and will not round. I ask why not simplify for teaching. He says you do not teach a child nineteen fingers because the twentieth is inconvenient.",
 "Andrannor. Every fashionable house here claims a rare type and half of them are painted on. The paint is honest work. The claim underneath it is not, and the animals know which is which.",
 "Veridan. Twenty types, and each stands over three and beneath three. Perfectly regular. The scribes show me the wheel and I understand for the first time that it is not a chart of strength. It is a chart of debt.",
 "Netharion. Twenty, and then the twenty-first, which the archive lists separately and calls ULTIMATE. It is not part of the wheel. It is exempt from it, and exemption is the most interesting word in this building.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy proves the wheel has exactly one legal completion. Every relationship it does not state is FORCED by the ones it does. Nobody chose those edges. They fell out.",
 "Xilnar. Type survives death. A Spirit-typed dead thing is still Spirit-typed and still refuses what Spirit refuses. Whatever type is, it is not a property of a body.",
 "Baelgor. The University teaches the wheel as biology. The Pledge treats it as law. Both are describing the same twenty words and only one of them can be right about what kind of thing they are.",
 "Thardin. They are trying to synthesise a type. Not a creature — a TYPE, a twenty-second entry. The wheel has one legal completion and they are trying to add a leg to a completed proof.",
 "Korathen. Twenty types plus one exempt from all of them. That is not a taxonomy. That is a court with twenty statutes and a single office that answers to none of them, and I have now been in the room where that office keeps its door."]),

("THE VOID SEAS","void",[
 "The Malezor coast is not a coast. It is an edge, and it is a hard one. The old men do not fish here and cannot tell me what they are not fishing for. The nets in the sheds are for rivers.",
 "Zarvane. There is no sea within four hundred miles and there is still a word for it here, and mothers use it. Do not go past the Void. Past what, out here? Past the last thing you can name.",
 "Andrannor. Something thrown into the Void does not float, does not sink, and does not come back. I watch a man dispose of evidence and I watch the Void agree to it, and I have not slept well since.",
 "Veridan. The scribes call the Void Seas the unwritten. Not empty — unwritten. This district describes the whole world in terms of what has and has not been set down, and only one thing gets that word.",
 "Netharion. The archive maps the Void Seas as an INTERSTITIAL, alongside the Wild March, the Green Divide and the Pit. They are not features of the world. They are the seams between its pieces.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy: matter entering the Void does not cease. It stops being ADDRESSED. The Matrix simply no longer has a line for it. It is not destruction. It is de-listing.",
 "Xilnar. Nothing lost to the Void arrives here. That is twice now this notebook has found somewhere the dead do not go, and both times it was somewhere I could point at on a map.",
 "Baelgor. The founders set the borders at the Void deliberately. The Pledge calls it the honest edge. They were not fencing the sea out. They were marking where their claim stopped being enforceable.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry surveys the Void with instruments that come back reading zero. Not error. Zero. They log that as a successful survey and the surveys continue on schedule.",
 "Korathen. The Void Seas are not water and not death. They are where the list does not reach. Everything in this notebook is about what is permitted to exist, and out there is the only place on this world where nothing has been permitted anything."]),

("THARDUN","thardun",[
 "A Thardinian object in a Malezor kitchen: the sphere on the shelf by the door. Nobody here has been to Thardin. Everybody here owns something made there and nobody finds that worth a remark.",
 "Zarvane. The caravans carry Thardinian goods and Zarvanian nothing. I ask what goes the other way. Silence, water, weather, respect. I write it as a joke and then I look at the list again.",
 "Andrannor. The scanobots are Thardinian. So are the gatelocks, and so is the reason nobody here can go where they please. This district thinks it is the free one.",
 "Veridan. Parliament imports Thardinian instruments to measure things Thardin cannot measure. The scribes find this funny in a way that takes me a season to understand, and it is not a kind kind of funny.",
 "Netharion. The archive: Thardun is not a company, a house or a state. It is the name for the fact that one district makes the objects the other nine relationships run through.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy will not accept Thardinian instruments for original work. The stated reason is calibration. The real reason, given to me in a corridor, is that they read what they were built to read.",
 "Xilnar. Thardinian devices do not function here. The dead find this hilarious, and it is the only thing I have found in this district that they will joke about.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge predates Thardun and does not mention it. Everything the founders built has since been retrofitted with Thardinian parts, and no revision was ever recorded.",
 "Thardin. Standing in it now. It is not sinister. It is a working city, honest and proud and enormously good at its trade, and that is exactly why nobody here can see the shape of the thing they have built.",
 "Korathen. Thardun made the vessel that binds a Zyrex to a Rizer. Every bond on this world, every partnership the Novarian Challenge will ever be judged on, completes through an object one district manufactures. Korathen oversees Thardin, and I no longer think that is an administrative arrangement."]),

("THE EMPTY THRONE","throne",[
 "Ten districts. Ten Gemlords. The Malezor almanac lists nine and leaves the tenth line ruled and blank, and it has been printed that way for as long as anyone can find a copy.",
 "Zarvane. There is a toast here that is drunk to nine and then a pause. Nobody drinks in the pause. I ask what it is for. For the one who is not at table, and the subject closes.",
 "Andrannor. A club with ten booths keeps the tenth roped. The management says renovation. The rope is older than the manager, and the velvet has been worn smooth by hands that stop there.",
 "Veridan. Parliament seats ten and has seated nine for longer than the record runs. The tenth chair is maintained. Somebody polishes it. There is a line in the budget for polishing it.",
 "Netharion. The archive names him. Oatheus. Tenth Gemlord, absent, not deposed and not dead — absent, which is a legal status here with its own paperwork, and the paperwork has no expiry.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy: an empty throne is not a vacancy. A vacancy can be filled. This one refuses candidates, and they have the records of eleven refusals, and none of the eleven were refused by a person.",
 "Xilnar. Oatheus is not among the dead. I have looked properly, twice. I know what it costs to look properly here, and I would go a third time if I believed it would help.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge was sworn by ten. The founders' hall has ten places and nine names carved. The tenth was left uncarved on purpose — the stone is dressed and finished and waiting.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry's Gemlord department has ten files. Nine are active. The tenth is open, empty, and has been requisitioned for new material every year for ninety years by a clerk following a standing order.",
 "Korathen. The Empty Throne is not a wound in this world's government. It is a countdown. Nine anchors hold and one does not, and everything I have written in this notebook has been circling the day the tenth is either filled or finally understood."]),

("THE MIGRATION","migration",[
 "There is a road out of Malezor that goes north and stops. It is well made, it is old, and it is aimed at something. Nobody built a road that good to end in a field.",
 "Zarvane. The oasis is a waypoint. Everything about it — the wells, the spacing, the customs of hospitality — is built for people passing through toward somewhere, and the somewhere is not named in any of it.",
 "Andrannor. The Alienlands begin here as a rumour and a change in the insects. The people of this district describe the north the way you describe a neighbour you have never spoken to.",
 "Veridan. The Seedvault holds Cytherion stock, catalogued as immigrant. Not invasive. Immigrant. A single word choice by a curator two hundred years dead, and it has held.",
 "Netharion. The archive is plain: they lost the Bug War and they came here. Spider and Mantis both, defeated and walking, into a world that had just woken up and had room.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy: the Migration was not resisted. Zyraxis did not fight them. Whatever the Verdant Awakening had made of this world, it had made something that could receive a defeated people.",
 "Xilnar. Their dead keep their own customs and their own quarter and have never assimilated. Six generations. The dead are the last to migrate and the slowest, and they are still arriving.",
 "Baelgor. The founders arrived AFTER the Migration and wrote their Pledge as though the land were empty. Every claim in that document is made over the heads of people already living here.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry classifies Alienlands populations as fauna. I have read the form. There is a box, and somebody ticks it, and the box has been the same box for ninety years.",
 "Korathen. Cytherion fell and its survivors walked to the ninth world, and the ninth world let them in. That is the single kindest fact in this notebook. It is also the reason the Seers can say this world is contaminated, and be believed."]),

("DREAMLAND","dream",[
 "Malezor children describe the same place when they are feverish. Blue light, no horizon, no fear. I write down four accounts from four families and three of them use the word ROOM.",
 "Zarvane. Sleep is treated as travel here. You are not asked whether you slept well. You are asked what you saw, and the asking is polite, ordinary, and completely serious.",
 "Andrannor. There is a drug in the clubs that people take to get there faster. It works and it takes them somewhere else, and the difference is obvious to everyone except the people taking it.",
 "Veridan. The scribes record dreams in the same ledgers as observations, in the same ink, with no separation. I ask which column is which. They say the question shows I have not been listening.",
 "Netharion. The archive calls it the Blue-Gem plane and files it with places, not with states of mind. Coordinates. Access conditions. A note about who has jurisdiction, left blank.",
 "Vorashil. The Academy: Dreamland is where a Rizer's Ultimate form is gated. Not learned there — GATED there. Something has to see you in that place before it will let you have it here.",
 "Xilnar. The dead dream. I do not know what to do with that and I am writing it anyway, because the whole point of a notebook is that you write it down before you know what to do with it.",
 "Baelgor. The Pledge was drafted after a shared dream. The University teaches this as a founding myth. The founders recorded it as a MEETING, with attendance, and I have seen the list.",
 "Thardin. The Ministry cannot instrument Dreamland and this offends them more than anything else I have raised. Every other mystery on this world has at least agreed to be measured badly.",
 "Korathen. Dreamland is not a place we go. It is the place where what we are is looked at without the body in the way, and everything I have found out here — the Matrix, the types, the throne — is that same act of being looked at, and finally I am too tired to pretend I do not know by whom."]),
]
